  "findings": [
    "The review was anchored to exact git objects rather than the dirty shared worktree. I inspected the mechanism account and Rust implementation with git show at implementation commit bec36e625e58711bbb1e32d878a31cb63b47c36d, inspected Java SkinParam at revision 71806a23780b04a5ccde2f8ceb5121edad5eb711, and rendered held-outs only through the supplied diff_one helper with SHA256 3183361f7ad8fa84df87d781ba1268857ffe55ea7be83b1a13c38a5df684d51b. No cargo or rustc commands were run.",
    "Java provenance still supports the claimed ordinary-key identity. SkinParam.cleanForKeySlow lowercases, strips underscores and dots, rewrites family-specific arrow prefixes to arrow, and rewrites a terminal align to alignment before lookup. Rust's parser canonical_skinparam_key matches that model, and commit bec36e6 threads it through state_skinparam_preferred_value, state_skinparam_value, StateArrowFont::from_skinparams, autonomous_outer_spacing, has_only_autonomous_layout_skinparams, and has_only_flat_label_skinparams.",
    "Static inspection of the one-file implementation diff found no fixture-shaped branches, no golden-data reads, no SVG string surgery, and no new unexplained parity constants. The change is a direct substitution from raw case-insensitive string comparison to parser-level canonical identity.",
    "All four fresh held-outs are valid and mechanism-shaped. They cover left-to-right versus top-to-bottom layout, small named Courier labels versus ordinary sans-serif labels, dotted and underscored spellings, stateArrow versus shared arrow prefixes, explicit reassignment order, and both value-resolution and painted-envelope capability-admission surfaces.",
    "Every fresh held-out passed strict no-oracle comparison against pinned Java. The two alias forms that were supposed to denote the same ordinary key also collapsed to identical Rust SVGs in each pair: the flat-label Courier pair hashes to 247a8bc82a3da2320b10eec9d4a48dc376680601fc94785b96adc5d6df876627, and the top-to-bottom default-alignment pair hashes to 4a3671b466c1634c33722602732657d3c95024fdc931b82fd72d584796646ace.",
    "I did not find an in-scope counterexample. Given the clean Java provenance, the absence of suspicious implementation patterns, four green no-oracle held-outs, and the pairwise Rust-output identity checks, this checker round supports the account's claim that ordinary state skinparam lookup and capability admission now compare canonical Java key identities rather than retained source spellings."
